title: Gallax Flees to the Empire!
subtitle: The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> disintegrates!
view-if: chancellor = "Staal" and staal_time == 9 and royalist_leader == "Gallax"
new-page: true
tags: event
max-visits: 1
on-display: {!  
    var cardEl = document.createElement('div');  
    cardEl.className = "face-figure2";  

    var image = new Image();  
    image.className = "face-img";  
    image.src = "img/hitler_dead.jpg";  

    cardEl.appendChild(image);
    var contentDiv = document.querySelector("#page #mid_panel #content");
    contentDiv.appendChild(cardEl);
!}

= Gallax Flees to the Empire!

Gallax himself has lost belief in his previously unshakable determination that destiny is on his side, and his appointment to the chancellorship is an inevitability. Now, with the defections of Glade and the majority of the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span>, and Crowde's resignation months back: the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> movement has lost its chance.

With the movement crumbling around him, Gallax has slipped across the border to the Empire-in-Exile, abandoning the Commonwealth he claimed to serve. The man who would set the Empress upon a restored throne has fled to her court—and in doing so has laid bare, at last, where his loyalties always lay.

- @nazi_2: The end of a movement.

@nazi_2
on-arrival: royalist_leader = "Standerton"; royalist_chancellor = "Gorrick"; gallax_dead = 1; dufour_gallax_r -= 10; papen_strength -= 2; staal_strength += 1; royalist_funds -= 3
achievement: gallax_tot

Alden Standerton succeeds Gallax as party leader, with heavy influence from Ulric Gorrick. With their founder's flight to the enemy now public, the movement is badly discredited, and likely never to regain prominence.